Relevant tables / columns for this task  

• Movie.MID : primary movie identifier, needed to connect a film to its cast  
• Movie.year : text field that contains the release‑year information (take last 4 chars → numeric year)  
• M_Cast.MID : movie identifier in the cast bridge table, lets us find every performer appearing in a film  
• M_Cast.PID : person identifier in the cast bridge table, used to reach the person’s gender  
• Person.PID : primary key for a performer, lets us join to M_Cast  
• Person.Gender : gender value for every performer – only the value 'Female' counts as female, all other
  values ('Male', 'None', NULL, etc.) count as non‑female  

Typical conditions you will use  

• substr(Movie.year, length(Movie.year) - 3)  – last 4 characters of the year column  
• Person.Gender = 'Female'                    – to keep only female performers  
• Person.Gender <> 'Female' OR Person.Gender IS NULL  – to spot any non‑female performer  
• GROUP BY Movie.MID / extracted_year         – when aggregating per movie or per year  

Below are 10 exploratory SQL statements (LIMIT 20 on each) that go from simple inspection to the full
percentage calculation.  
Each statement is preceded by a short description.

```sql
-- 1. List a few raw year strings exactly as stored in Movie.year
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM Movie
LIMIT 20;

-- 2. Show how the 4‑digit year can be extracted and cast to INTEGER
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(substr(year, length(year) - 3) AS INTEGER) AS release_year
FROM Movie
LIMIT 20;

-- 3. Pair every movie with its extracted 4‑digit year
SELECT MID, title, CAST(substr(year, length(year) - 3) AS INTEGER) AS release_year
FROM Movie
LIMIT 20;

-- 4. See how many cast members each movie has (no gender filter yet)
SELECT m.MID,
       m.title,
       COUNT(c.PID) AS cast_cnt
FROM Movie AS m
LEFT JOIN M_Cast AS c ON m.MID = c.MID
GROUP BY m.MID
LIMIT 20;

-- 5. For each movie, count how many male / female / unknown actors it has
SELECT m.MID,
       SUM(CASE WHEN p.Gender = 'Female' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS female_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN p.Gender = 'Male'   THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS male_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN p.Gender NOT IN ('Male','Female') OR p.Gender IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS unk_cnt
FROM Movie AS m
LEFT JOIN M_Cast AS c ON m.MID = c.MID
LEFT JOIN Person  AS p ON c.PID = p.PID
GROUP BY m.MID
LIMIT 20;

-- 6. Return the movies that have at least one male or unknown performer
SELECT DISTINCT m.MID
FROM Movie AS m
JOIN   M_Cast AS c ON m.MID = c.MID
JOIN   Person  AS p ON c.PID = p.PID
WHERE  p.Gender <> 'Female' OR p.Gender IS NULL
LIMIT 20;

-- 7. Identify the movies that have *only* female performers
SELECT m.MID, m.title
FROM Movie AS m
WHERE m.MID NOT IN (
      SELECT mc.MID
      FROM M_Cast AS mc
      JOIN Person  AS p ON mc.PID = p.PID
      WHERE p.Gender <> 'Female' OR p.Gender IS NULL
)
LIMIT 20;

-- 8. Count total movies released in each year
SELECT CAST(substr(year, length(year) - 3) AS INTEGER) AS release_year,
       COUNT(*) AS total_movies
FROM Movie
GROUP BY release_year
LIMIT 20;

-- 9. Count exclusively‑female‑cast movies in each year
WITH female_only AS (
   SELECT m.MID
   FROM Movie AS m
   WHERE m.MID NOT IN (
         SELECT mc.MID
         FROM M_Cast AS mc
         JOIN Person AS p ON mc.PID = p.PID
         WHERE p.Gender <> 'Female' OR p.Gender IS NULL
   )
)
SELECT CAST(substr(m.year, length(m.year) - 3) AS INTEGER) AS release_year,
       COUNT(*) AS female_only_movies
FROM Movie AS m
JOIN female_only fo ON m.MID = fo.MID
GROUP BY release_year
LIMIT 20;

-- 10. Combine totals and female‑only counts to compute the percentage per year
WITH female_only AS (
   SELECT m.MID
   FROM Movie AS m
   WHERE m.MID NOT IN (
         SELECT mc.MID
         FROM M_Cast AS mc
         JOIN Person AS p ON mc.PID = p.PID
         WHERE p.Gender <> 'Female' OR p.Gender IS NULL
   )
),
totals AS (
   SELECT CAST(substr(year, length(year) - 3) AS INTEGER) AS release_year,
          COUNT(*) AS total_movies
   FROM Movie
   GROUP BY release_year
),
fo_cnt AS (
   SELECT CAST(substr(m.year, length(m.year) - 3) AS INTEGER) AS release_year,
          COUNT(*) AS female_only_movies
   FROM Movie AS m
   JOIN female_only fo ON m.MID = fo.MID
   GROUP BY release_year
)
SELECT t.release_year,
       t.total_movies,
       ROUND(100.0 * COALESCE(f.female_only_movies,0) / t.total_movies, 2) AS pct_female_only
FROM totals t
LEFT JOIN fo_cnt f ON t.release_year = f.release_year
ORDER BY t.release_year
LIMIT 20;
```

These steps take you from basic data inspection to the final computation of the yearly percentage of films whose cast is exclusively female.
